ing combined I just I don't  really understand what the impetus was  for this tweet I mean maybe it does have  to do with the g20 but like you could  have said this all along that's what's  very strange about it and it's the  timing that is making me wonder what the  hell is going on and along those lines I  have sort of like one more hypothesis to  present to you which is a little bit  more involved than the ones I've  mentioned so far let's imagine that  Donald Trump realizes that at some point  he's gonna have to make a call about  whether the United States gets involved  in Ukraine or not because as you may  remember Russia's aggression against  Ukraine has been increasing they rammed  a Ukrainian Navy vessel they took and  haven't returned at least as at the last  time that I looked some Ukrainian Navy  sailors almost every other Western  country has come out in defense of  Ukraine if you're Trump and you are  realizing that at some point you might  have to say we're going to get involved  with our allies in defending Ukraine or  we're not what about the possibility of  laying the groundwork now for saying you  know what we can't afford to get  involved to help Ukraine because we're  spending so much on the military just  like I tweeted after the g20 is that  type of forethought possible for Trump I  think so and you know this is why he  takes every possible position on every  possible issue because people can just  pick and choose his comments well he or  he said that he wants more defense  spending and here he says he wants less  defense spending so you can just pick  and choose what fits your political  ideology and that's what his supporters  do to be super clear I agree with Trump  that military spending is out of control  I don't want to pretend like all of a  sudden now that Trump says it it's not  what I believe I agree with him it's  just he's almost always tweeting the  opposite of this sentiment and I'm  trying to figure out what is it that's  going 